---
import { isPageMounted } from "../../lib/sitePages";
import { normalizeValidatorContact } from "../validator/lib/validatorContact";

const contactRaw = import.meta.env.VALIDATOR_CONTACT;
const contactInput =
  typeof contactRaw === "string" ? contactRaw.trim() : String(contactRaw ?? "").trim();

if (isPageMounted("validator") && contactInput === "") {
  throw new Error("VALIDATOR_CONTACT is required when the validator page is mounted");
}

const contactLink =
  contactInput === "" ? null : normalizeValidatorContact(contactInput);

// Defaults from opencloudmesh-go/internal/platform/store/validatorcore/session_config.go
const sessionLimit = 16;
const maxDriveIdleSeconds = 1800;
const terminalRetentionDays = 30;

// Public start rate limit from opencloudmesh-go/internal/platform/config/presets.go
const startPublicRequests = 10;
const startPublicWindowSeconds = 60;

const idleMinutes = Math.floor(maxDriveIdleSeconds / 60);
---

<aside
  class="space-y-4 rounded-2xl border border-amber-900/50 bg-amber-950/20 p-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-amber-100/90"
  aria-label="Validator service notice"
>
  <h2 class="text-base font-semibold text-amber-50">Public validator notice</h2>

  <p>
    This service runs at ocm.azadehafzar.io. It is a same-origin JSON validator
    that performs external probes against your target and returns a graded
    report.
  </p>

  <p>
    This validator accepts anonymous, unauthenticated scan requests from the
    public internet. Each client IP may start at most {startPublicRequests} new
    sessions every {startPublicWindowSeconds} seconds. Outbound probe traffic
    uses strict SSRF controls: private addresses, link-local targets, and other
    disallowed destinations are rejected.
  </p>

  <p>
    Concurrent driving work is capped at {sessionLimit} sessions per validator
    process. Only one active run is allowed per target at a time; different
    targets may run concurrently (v1.3.1). An idle active drive is interrupted
    after {maxDriveIdleSeconds} seconds
    ({idleMinutes} minutes) without progress. Terminal report rows are retained
    for about {terminalRetentionDays} days unless you opt in to a permanent
    report tier at start time.
  </p>

  <p>
    Statistics contribution and active validation are opt-in at start time and
    default to off. Statistics are published only when explicitly opted in and
    only after a k-anonymity threshold of 5 is met. Active validation appears
    only when the service manifest
    exposes the required opt-in field. Passive results are informational, not a
    certification, and may miss platform-specific behavior or time-limited
    failures.
  </p>

  <p>
    Out of scope: inbound OCM, user accounts, OAuth, alerts, and unrelated
    Matrix features.
  </p>

  <p>
    Operator contact:
    {contactLink?.ok === true && (
      <a
        class="text-sky-300 underline-offset-2 hover:text-sky-200 hover:underline"
        href={contactLink.href}
      >
        {contactLink.label}
      </a>
    )}
  </p>
</aside>
